## 2. Rocket Propulsion Engineering (Tsiolkovsky Equation)

### Propellant Mass Ratio & Staging Requirement
Relates spacecraft velocity change $\Delta v$ to engine exhaust efficiency (Specific Impulse $I_{sp}$) and initial-to-final mass ratio:

$$\Delta v = I_{sp} \cdot g_0 \cdot \ln\left(\frac{m_0}{m_f}\right)$$

Solving for required propellant mass $m_{\text{propellant}} = m_0 - m_f$:

$$m_{\text{propellant}} = m_f \left(e^{\frac{\Delta v}{I_{sp} \cdot g_0}} - 1\right)$$

* $I_{sp}$: Specific impulse of the propulsion stage ($\text{s}$)
* $g_0 = 9.80665\text{ m/s}^2$: Standard Earth gravitational acceleration
* $m_0$: Wet mass at ignition ($\text{kg}$); $m_f$: Dry stage mass + payload mass ($\text{kg}$)

