## 3. Entry, Descent & Landing (NASA-SP-8013)

### Ballistic Coefficient ($\beta$) & Terminal Descent Velocity
Models aerodynamic deceleration during planetary atmospheric entry:

$$\beta = \frac{m}{C_D \cdot A}, \qquad v_{\text{terminal}} = \sqrt{\frac{2 \beta g}{\rho}}$$

* $C_D$: Aerodynamic drag coefficient
* $A$: Reference cross-sectional heat-shield area ($\text{m}^2$)
* $\rho$: Local atmospheric density ($\text{kg/m}^3$)

