## 4. Quantum-Inspired Mission Optimization (QUBO Hamiltonian)

### Combinatorial Propulsion & Budget Optimization
Formulates discrete rocket stage selection under mass and financial budget constraints as a Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) energy minimization problem:

$$H(x) = \sum_{i} m_{\text{prop}, i} \, x_i + P \left(\sum_{i} x_i - 1\right)^2 + \lambda_{\text{budget}} \max\left(0, \sum_{i} C_i x_i - C_{\max}\right)^2$$

* $x_i \in \{0, 1\}$: Binary decision variable selecting propulsion architecture $i$
* $P$: One-hot constraint penalty ensuring exactly one propulsion system is selected
* $C_i, C_{\max}$: Stage cost and maximum mission budget threshold ($\text{USD Millions}$)

